# =============================================================================
# DOCUMENTATION HEADER — DAG Planner — user prompt template
# =============================================================================
# This header is documentation for maintainers. The runtime loader reads the
# entire file (including these lines) into the LLM prompt string. Keep the
# original instructional sections below unchanged in meaning and order.
#
# SECTION: Placeholders
#   {goal_id}, {goal_description}, {agent_context}, {goal_prefix} filled by DAGPlanner.plan().
#
# SECTION: Goal block
#   States which single goal this DAG is for.
#
# SECTION: Agent context
#   Injected AVAILABLE AGENTS summary from BasePlanner.
#
# SECTION: ID rules
#   Require goal_prefix + nodeX ids and matching depends_on references.
#
# SECTION: Parallelism
#   Ask for deps only when truly needed.
#
# =============================================================================
GOAL ID: {goal_id}
GOAL DESCRIPTION: {goal_description}

{agent_context}

Generate a DAG-based plan where tasks can depend on any number of previous tasks.
For tasks with no dependencies, use an empty depends_on list.

Important: 
1. Create a unique ID for each node using the format: "{goal_prefix}nodeX" 
   where X is a sequential number (e.g., "{goal_prefix}node0", "{goal_prefix}node1")

2. When specifying dependencies in 'depends_on', use these same node IDs

3. Make sure to set the goal_id to {goal_id} for all nodes in this plan

4. Maximize parallelism where possible by only creating dependencies when truly needed
